  "local_patches": [
    "In `src/stroke.rs`, `StrokeCtx::do_linear` skips a cusp, or the end point, whose tangent from the point before it is exactly zero, instead of passing the tangent to `do_join` and `do_line`, which divide by its length, so a collinear cubic whose cusps round onto the point before them or onto its end point no longer gives NaN coordinates. The test `stroke::tests::linear_cubic_with_coincident_cusps` covers it.",
    "In `src/stroke.rs`, the stroker skips a quadratic or cubic whose start or end tangent from `PathSeg::tangents` is zero, as it skips a zero-length line, so a closed loop with control arms shorter than 1e-6 no longer gives NaN coordinates; a quadratic's own tangents are passed on to `do_cubic` and `do_linear`, since the cubic it raises to has control arms 2/3 as long. The test `stroke::tests::tiny_closed_loops` covers it."
  ],
